research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-193-- **The witness is not exotic.** It is the first series a reader meets whose convergence depends on cancellation, and the failure is as large as it can be: the series of absolute values does not merely converge to a different number, it diverges to $+\infty$.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-194-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-convergent-implies-absolutely-convergent.prompt.md-195-- **Everything on this page turns on this example.** Because the class of conditionally convergent series is nonempty, [[thm-riemann-series-theorem]] has content, and [[cor-unconditional-iff-absolute-in-r]] separates two genuinely different properties rather than restating one. The same series, with its rearrangements, is developed on the companion page.
