research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-alternating-harmonic-rearranged-to-three-halves.prompt.md-2103-- The divergence test is the standard way to show a concrete sequence diverges, and it is how [[fs-bounded-implies-convergent]] is refuted. The opposite direction, extracting a convergent subsequence from a bounded sequence, is Bolzano-Weierstrass; it is **not available at this point in the reading order**, being the subject of the next page of this track, *Monotone Sequences, Bolzano-Weierstrass, and Cauchy Completeness*, where it is proved.
